    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "When you’re trying to stay seated, do you get an uncomfortable restless feeling in your legs?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S010",
      "patient_response": "Well, I don't know if it's an uncomfortable feeling exactly, but my legs are definitely always busy. Like when I'm sitting at my desk grading essays—and oh, don't even get me started on the essays this year. The grammar is just atrocious. I don't know what they teach them in middle school anymore, but it certainly isn't punctuation! I had one student, bless his heart, who wrote an entire page about the French Revolution as a single run-on sentence. \n\nBut anyway, when I'm sitting there trying to get through the grading, or even when I'm in church on Sundays, I'll catch myself tapping my foot constantly. Or I'll be clicking my red pen, just click-click-click, and shifting around in my seat so much that I actually have to stop and remind myself to just settle down. The pews at our church are terribly hard, though. They haven't replaced the cushions since the late nineties, I swear. My husband always insists on sitting on the aisle because he likes the legroom, but I just end up squirming through the whole sermon.",
