    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "When you feel like you can’t stay seated, do you also feel worried or on edge?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Worried? Oh, no, I wouldn't say that. I don't feel nervous or anxious when I can't stay in my chair, it's just... well, I just feel like I need to be doing something. Though, speaking of being on edge, the only thing that really has me worried lately is the upcoming school board meeting. They’re talking about cutting funding for the music programs, which is just an absolute tragedy. I mean, my niece plays the cello, and she is phenomenal—just absolutely phenomenal. She’s actually looking at conservatories for next year. Juilliard, Peabody... we’re all so proud of her. \n\nMy sister spent a small fortune on private lessons, of course, driving her all the way to Boston every single weekend. The traffic on I-90 is just dreadful, especially in the summer with all the tourists heading to the Cape. I told her she should just take the train, but she insists she needs the car for the instrument. \n\nBut anyway, what were we saying? Oh, right. No, I don't feel worried or on edge in my own head when I'm getting up from my desk or the table. I just can't seem to stay put.",
