    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Is this urge to move your legs worse in the evening or at night?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Worse in the evening? No, I haven't noticed it being worse then. It's pretty much the same no matter what time it is, just whenever I'm stuck sitting. \n\nThough, to be honest, by the time evening actually rolls around, I'm usually so exhausted from dealing with the teenagers all day that I just collapse in my favorite armchair. My husband and I have been watching that new British mystery series on PBS—oh, the one set in the Cotswolds? It is just delightful. The scenery is absolutely gorgeous, though it is a bit ridiculous how many people get murdered in such a tiny village. You'd think the property values would absolutely plummet! We actually went to England for our 25th anniversary, rented a little cottage not far from Bath. It rained the entire time, of course, but the scones... oh, the scones over there are to die for. I've tried baking them at home, but they never turn out quite right. I think it's the butter we have here, it just doesn't have the same fat content, you know? \n\nWait, what was the question? Oh! My legs. Right. No, it's not worse at night at all. Just... whenever I have to stay put.",
