      "patient_response": "Energized? Euphoric? Oh, heavens no. I don't think I've had a day where I felt euphoric since... well, maybe my wedding day. Or the day I finally got my master's degree! That was a relief, let me tell you. Writing that thesis nearly did me in. I wrote it on the symbolism in 19th-century American literature, specifically Nathaniel Hawthorne. You know, everyone focuses on *The Scarlet Letter*, but his short stories are really where he shines. *Young Goodman Brown*? Brilliant. I try to get my sophomores to appreciate it, but getting them to read anything that isn't on a screen these days is like pulling teeth. \n\nI actually confiscated three cell phones just yesterday during second period. Three! And then the parents complain when the kids miss the material. One mother emailed me at 11:00 PM on a Tuesday demanding to know why her son got a C on his paper. 11:00 PM! As if I don't have a life outside of school. I was right in the middle of a very intense game of Scrabble with my husband, too. I had the letters for 'quixotic' but nowhere to play it. Such a shame. \n\nBut no, to answer your question, I don't get unusually energized for days at a time. I'm just my regular self, trying to keep up with everything.",
